# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Wallpapers (add your own, don't commit large binaries)
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.jpg
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.jpeg
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.png
# wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*.webp
# !wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/.gitkeep

# Theme engine runtime output (PIPE-03/D-05) — generated colors live in
# ~/.local/state/theme/, outside this repo. yazi has no native
# @import/include mechanism (D-07) so theme-engine wires its config path
# directly with a symlink into the state dir; since it lives under a
# whole-package stow symlink back into this repo tree, the symlink
# theme-apply creates lands at this exact repo-relative path — ignore it.
# (The retired external launcher's own equivalent ignore rule was removed
# in quick task 260822-sht Task 11 along with its direct-wiring symlink.)
yazi/.config/yazi/theme.toml

# Screenshots (D-48) — runtime output from screenshot.sh, never repo content.
# Belt-and-suspenders alongside the .stow-local-ignore fold exclusion above.
wallpapers/Pictures/Screenshots/

# Live wallpapers (AMB-01/D-02) — video/animated-image files a user drops
# into ~/Pictures/Wallpapers/<theme>/live/ to play as a live wallpaper.
# User-side media, never repo content; large binaries must never land in
# git history. stow.sh pre-creates the directory itself (real, not a repo
# path) so the layout reproduces without ever needing to track a file here.
wallpapers/Pictures/Wallpapers/*/live/

# GSD research cache — ephemeral web-research cache written by the research
# skill/tool, never meant to be tracked (CLEAN-02/D-50 git-clean invariant).
.planning/research/.cache/

# container-run.sh runtime logs (03-04) — machine-readable evidence written
# per invocation under verify/logs/run-<timestamp>/, never repo content.
verify/logs/

# container-run.sh host-cache reuse (22-09 perf) — persistent, container-
# writable pacman/paru cache directories the gate accumulates across runs.
# Real package/build artifacts, never repo content; regenerated by any run
# that isn't --cold.
verify/cache/

# Desktop entries (stow-symlink side effect). vscodium/.local/share/applications/
# is stow-symlinked to ~/.local/share/applications/, so any app that registers a
# launcher (Steam, Lutris, installers) writes its .desktop straight into this repo
# and trips theme-doctor's clean-tree gate. Ignore by default; the entries we
# deliberately version are opted back in below.
vscodium/.local/share/applications/*
!vscodium/.local/share/applications/codium.desktop
!vscodium/.local/share/applications/claude-code-url-handler.desktop
# Terminal-app wrappers: xdg-open never reads Terminal=true, so the packaged
# yazi/nvim entries open no window when set as default handlers. These two
# are Terminal=false and route through /usr/local/bin/open-in-terminal.
!vscodium/.local/share/applications/yazi-terminal.desktop
!vscodium/.local/share/applications/nvim-terminal.desktop

# Python bytecode cache (260818-u6v). theme-engine/lib/fastfetch-sprites.py is
# this repo's first Python file, and theme-engine/lib is stow-symlinked to
# ~/.config/theme-engine/lib — so anything that *imports* the module (rather
# than exec'ing it, which is what theme_engine_fastfetch_regen does via
# `python3 "$FASTFETCH_SPRITES_PY"`) drops a __pycache__/ straight into this
# repo and trips theme-doctor's clean-tree gate. A py_compile syntax check
# does exactly that. Never repo content.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# GSD run-scoped dispatch-isolation sentinel. Written by gsd-tools on every
# agent dispatch so the isolation guard hooks can read the resolved mode; it
# is session-local state, not repo content, and its presence trips
# theme-doctor's clean-tree gate. Same class as __pycache__/ above.
.gsd/
